uration and temperature not specified unless stated. Not a chemical design limit.","type":"Manufacturer statement","at":"Effect of strong alkalis","reads":"contrary"}]},{"category":"oil-grease","meaning":"Oil and grease resistance","items":[{"product":"Polymaker HT PLA GF","verdict":"resistant","text":"Good","source":"S-POLYCN-Polymaker-HT-PLA-GF-TDS-EN-V1-1","id":"Q00078","productId":"G019-01","topic":"Effect of oils and grease","agent":null,"strength":"unspecified","conditions":"p. 2; concentration, duration and temperature not specified unless stated. Not a chemical design limit.","type":"Manufacturer statement","at":"Effect of oils and grease","reads":"positive"}]},{"category":"fatigue","meaning":"Fatigue evidence","items":[{"product":null,"verdict":"no verdict","text":"Fibre reinforcement does not guarantee improved fatigue life. Matrix damage, fibre alignment, moisture and cyclic heating can govern endurance.","source":"LOCAL-FATIGUE","id":"Q00319","productId":null,"topic":"Shared reinforced-polymer principle","agent":null,"strength":"Not applicable","conditions":"Applies to reinforced entries; not an FDM fatigue allowable.","type":"Selection interpretation","at":"Shared reinforced-polymer principle","reads":"unread"}]}],"guide":null,"resin":{"polymer":"PLA","exposures":[{"meaning":"Organic solvent resistance","items":[{"agent":"Chloroform","verdict":"not-resistant","text":"Of the solvents studied, chloroform is the best solvent for quickly preparing 10 % wt/vol solutions of all Ingeo grades and morphologies; 4032D pellets and injection-moulded bars were readily transformed to 10 % wt/vol solutions in chloroform in 2-4 hours at room temperature","source":"R-NATUREWORKS-INGEO-SOLUBILITY","id":"PB00001","conditions":"10 % wt/vol mixture, shaken at 175 rpm at room temperature; some samples stirred at 65 °C","note":"Study grades: 4060D (12 % D, amorphous), 2003D (4.5 % D) and 4032D (1.6 % D, crystallisable) as pellets and injection-moulded bars; no filament grade was tested. A printed part is largely amorphous, so the amorphous-bar results are the nearer case. The reference reports dissolution; the verdict word \"soluble\" is reserved for water, so dissolution in an organic solvent is recorded as not-resistant.","at":"p. 2 Results (4032D); p. 3 Conclusions","screens":true},{"agent":"Tetrahydrofuran (THF)","verdict":"not-resistant","text":"4060D fully dissolved at room temperature; the amorphous injection-moulded 2003D bar reached an 8.5 % wt/vol solution in THF at room temperature (crystalline 2003D pellets 0.8 %); 4032D at 65 °C reached 9.31 wt% (pellets, 1 day) and 6.58 wt% (bar, 1 day) total lactic acid equivalents, Table 3","source":"R-NATUREWORKS-INGEO-SOLUBILITY","id":"PB00002","conditions":"10 % wt/vol mixture, shaken at 175 rpm at room temperature; some samples stirred at 65 °C","note":"Study grades: 4060D (12 % D, amorphous), 2003D (4.5 % D) and 4032D (1.6 % D, crystallisable) as pellets and injection-moulded bars; no filament grade was tested. A printed part is largely amorphous, so the amorphous-bar results are the nearer case. The reference reports dissolution; the verdict word \"soluble\" is reserved for water, so dissolution in an organic solvent is recorded as not-resistant.","at":"p. 2 Figure 1; p. 3 Table 3 and 2003D paragraph","screens":true},{"agent":"Acetone","verdict":"limited","text":"4060D fully dissolved at room temperature. For 4032D none of the solvents other than chloroform dissolved significant quantities at room temperature (all solutions < 1 wt% total acid equivalents up to 10 days), but the low-crystallinity bars turned from clear to cloudy, indicating that the material crystallised as a consequence of solvent plasticisation; at 65 °C acetone gave 0.29 wt% (pellets) and 0.86 wt% (bar), Table 3","source":"R-NATUREWORKS-INGEO-SOLUBILITY","id":"PB00003","conditions":"10 % wt/vol mixture, shaken at 175 rpm at room temperature; some samples stirred at 65 °C","note":"Study grades: 4060D (12 % D, amorphous), 2003D (4.5 % D) and 4032D (1.6 % D, crystallisable) as pellets and injection-moulded bars; no filament grade was tested. A printed part is largely amorphous, so the amorphous-bar results are the nearer case. The reference reports dissolution; the verdict word \"soluble\" is reserved for water, so dissolution in an organic solvent is recorded as not-resistant.","at":"p. 2 Results; p. 3 Table 3","screens":false},{"agent":"Toluene","verdict":"limited","text":"4060D dissolves fully at room temperature, with the slowest dissolution of the solvents tested. For 4032D toluene gave 0.08 wt% (pellets) and 0.06 wt% (bar) total lactic acid equivalents at 65 °C, Table 3; solvent plasticisation and crystallisation were observed during attempted dissolution","source":"R-NATUREWORKS-INGEO-SOLUBILITY","id":"PB00004","conditions":"10 % wt/vol mixture, shaken at 175 rpm at room temperature; some samples stirred at 65 °C","note":"Study grades: 4060D (12 % D, amorphous), 2003D (4.5 % D) and 4032D (1.6 % D, crystallisable) as pellets and injection-moulded bars; no filament grade was tested. A printed part is largely amorphous, so the amorphous-bar results are the nearer case. The reference reports dissolution; the verdict word \"soluble\" is reserved for water, so dissolution in an organic solvent is recorded as not-resistant.","at":"p. 2 Figure 1 paragraph; p. 3 Table 3","screens":false}],"category":"organic-solvent","verdict":"not-resistant","screens":true},{"meaning":"Flammability","items":[{"agent":"Combustibility (burning behaviour)","verdict":"not-resistant","text":"Ingeo biopolymers will burn. Clear to white smoke is produced when product burns. Toxic fumes are released under conditions of incomplete combustion.","source":"R-NATUREWORKS-INGEO-SOLUBILITY","id":"PB00005","conditions":null,"note":"No UL 94 rating is stated. Verdict convention used in this table: burns / UL 94 HB = not-resistant, V-1 or V-2 = limited, V-0 = resistant.","at":"p. 4 Safety and Handling Considerations, Combustibility","screens":true}],"category":"flammability","verdict":"not-resistant","screens":true},{"meaning":"Moisture sensitivity","items":[{"agent":"Moisture content before melt processing","verdict":"absorbs","text":"In-line drying is required. A moisture content of less than 0.025 % (250 ppm) is recommended to prevent viscosity degradation. Typical drying conditions are 4 hours at 80 °C (175 °F) to a dew point of -40 °C (-40 °F).","source":"R-NATUREWORKS-INGEO-3D850-TDS","id":"PB00006","conditions":"In-line drying before extrusion","note":"A processing threshold (hydrolytic loss of melt viscosity), not an equilibrium water uptake; the percentage in the finding is the recommended maximum before melting.","at":"p. 2 Drying","screens":false}],"category":"moisture","verdict":"limited","screens":false}]},"sources":[{"id":"I-ISANMATE-FORMNEXT-BLOG-PAGE","publisher":"iSANMATE","title":"iSANMATE Brings New Glass Fiber Series to Formnext Shenzhen","date":null,"read":"2026-09-26","kind":"Manufacturer product page or guide","url":"https://www.isanmate.com/isanmate-formnext-blog/","note":"The maker's own page, found by the research package of while re-reading a recorded conflict; consulted to confirm or explain it, and no value is transcribed from it."},{"id":"I-PLA-Glass-Fiber-Technical-Data-Sheet","publisher":"iSANMATE","title":"PLA Glass Fiber","date":null,"read":"2026-09-10","kind":"Manufacturer TDS","url":"https://www.isanmate.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/PLA-Glass-Fiber-Technical-Data-Sheet.pdf"},{"id":"LOCAL-FATIGUE","publisher":"User-supplied reference","title":"Plastics Engineering: fatigue of reinforced plastics","date":null,"read":"2026-09-10","kind":"Reference or register","url":null,"note":"A local reference, kept as provenance.","local":true},{"id":"PR-pla","publisher":"Prusa Research","title":"PLA | Prusa Knowledge Base","date":null,"read":"2026-09-10","kind":"Manufacturer product page or guide","url":"https://help.prusa3d.com/article/pla_2062"},{"